  "credentials": {
    "storage": "env var > OS keyring (optional) > <LOOPER_HOME|~/.config/looper>/credentials.env (mode 0600)",
    "never_in_config": true,
    "display": "mask all but last 4 chars"
  },
  "assignment_algorithm": [
    "1. Team = configured agents (1..max_agents). Each agent: kind cli|api|local, provider, model, tier.",
    "2. Tier: manual 'tier' wins; kind=cli or first-party API (anthropic/openai/xai/google) -> 'frontier'; else effective_params = total (dense) or sqrt(total*active) (MoE) from server metadata or the model name; pick the first tier (by rank, excluding frontier) whose max_params_b > effective_params; unknown size -> defaults.unknown_local_tier.",
    "3. For each stage: abstract = roles[stage.role].abstract. Capable = members whose tier.roles contains abstract (orchestrator also needs tier.can_orchestrate) and whose own roles list (if any) contains it.",
    "4. Order capable: roles with tools=true put tool-capable agents (CLIs) first. lead roles: higher tier rank, then strategy preference, then team order. Other roles: strategy preference, then higher rank, then team order.",
    "5. Diversity: if roles[role].diverse_from names an abstract role and the top candidate produced that role's last output, promote the next capable agent whose rank >= producer rank - 1.",
    "6. Nobody capable: optional pre/post stage -> skip; mergeable pre/post stage whose previous stage is a single stage in the same segment -> append its prompt to that stage; else assign the highest-rank member and mark under_tier.",
    "7. Lite mode: if the strongest member's tier rank <= rank('small'), skip all optional pre/post stages.",
    "8. parallel (Best-of-N): n = min(stage.n, distinct capable, max_best_of_n). One capable agent: if kind is api/local and tier.best_of_n -> n = min(stage.n, single_agent_samples) at temperatures spread 0.2..0.9; else n = 1 and the judge acts as self-critique.",
    "9. map (Orchestrator->Workers): max_items = min(stage.max_items, max tier.max_map_items of capable workers); <=3 if the orchestrator stage was under_tier; one-member team -> sequential; local workers -> at most max_parallel_local concurrent calls per local server.",
    "10. Iterations: loop max_iterations x min(tier.iteration_multiplier of body-stage agents), ceil, min 1.",
    "11. Prompts: whole prompt clipped (head+tail) to int(context_tokens*chars_per_token*context_fill) when the agent declares a window (context_window/num_ctx/context_tokens; may exceed tier.max_context_chars), else tier.max_context_chars; tiers with simplify_prompts get a short 'do one thing' prefix; text-only agents on tool roles get a 'propose diffs/commands, do not claim execution' prefix; map sources on tiers with structured_output unreliable|fair are asked for a numbered list.",
    "12. Team size: hard cap defaults.max_agents (5); warn above defaults.recommended_agents (3)."
  ],
  "degradation_order": [
    "skip optional",
    "merge into previous single stage",
    "under_tier on strongest member"
  ],
  "stage_flags": {
    "optional": "may be skipped",
    "mergeable": "may be folded into the previous stage"
  }
}
